From 3d461a534d39af5a4d31abfacf50e3a3374bc9fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:12:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge, VideoPlayer: a base layer in BT.1886 (profile 8.2)
 composed as CCM 001 clause 5.5 says, or not at all

ETSI GS CCM 001 composes a base layer in Recommendation ITU-R BT.1886, the
SDR base layer of Dolby Vision profile 8.2, at 14 bits and converts the
picture to SMPTE ST 2084 (clauses 5.4.3.3 and 5.5). Nothing told the bridge
the transfer of the base layer: such a picture was composed as if its base
layer were in PQ, natively and as HDR10.

The pictures of a stream whose Dolby Vision record says base layer
signal compatibility 2 (DVBRIDGE::BaseLayerIsSdr(): profiles 8.2, 9.2 and
10.2, also one whose record Kodi makes from the RPU) carry it
(VideoPicture::doviBaseSdr), through the renderer's buffer to the layer the
bridge draws (CDVBridgeGLES::Layer::baseSdr), for native output, its
warm-up, the renderer that checks its bytes and Dolby Vision as HDR10. The
bridge tells libplacebo (dvbridge_render_set_base_sdr(),
pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer of libplacebo-9955), whose composer
then does what the clauses say, or refuses the picture; libplacebo's own
reshaping never composes it.

Fail closed: where the picture is not composed so (the expert setting of
libplacebo's reshaping, or a reason libplacebo logs), nothing of it is
drawn, never a picture composed as if PQ. Native output then gives up
after its two seconds of frames that could not be shown, and Dolby Vision
as HDR10 after its 48 pictures, and the video goes on as Kodi plays it,
from its SDR base layer, which is a picture by itself. kodi.log says it:
the line of the first picture of a stream (its base layer is SDR and how
it is composed), libplacebo's line (why it was not), and the line that
disables native output names the reason; the Dolby Vision page of the
player information gives it as its reason (31874, en_gb and the three
Spanish languages). Every other stream is drawn as before.

Needs libplacebo-9955. Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink on
lavapipe): the bridge's render test (36 drawings, full raster and its
half, with the composer of CCM 001 and with libplacebo's reshaping) and its
fidelity bench (14 pictures of the profile 7 FEL test stream: source and
converted transport, libplacebo's reshaping, the 1080p half, the picture for
HDR10) give the same lines and files byte for byte as before; with the base
layer marked SDR the bridge draws the picture composed by clause 5.5, and
with libplacebo's reshaping it refuses it and libplacebo says why.
