  * reshaping, as before, to compare on hardware. A picture outside the clause's scope is composed
  * by libplacebo's reshaping either way (libplacebo logs why). */
 void dvbridge_render_use_ccm_composer(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer, bool use);
+/* Hades: the base layer of the pictures that follow is SDR, in Recommendation ITU-R BT.1886 (a Dolby
+ * Vision configuration with base layer signal compatibility 2: profile 8.2). ETSI GS CCM 001 then
+ * composes its samples at 14 bits and converts them to SMPTE ST 2084 (clause 5.5), which libplacebo
+ * does (pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer, libplacebo-9955); where it does not (the setting of
+ * libplacebo's reshaping, or a reason that libplacebo logs), the picture is not drawn, never one
+ * composed as if the base layer were in PQ. Off when a renderer is made. */
+void dvbridge_render_set_base_sdr(struct dvbridge_renderer *renderer, bool sdr);
+/* Hades: the last render of a picture whose base layer is SDR (above) failed because libplacebo did
+ * not compose it as clause 5.5 says */
